    "reason": "The $100 budget is shared with example-b, and the two campaigns split it evenly at about $50 each. example-a returned a ROAS of 4.0 ($200 revenue on $50 spend) every day for 30 days, with a CPA of $25. That is more than twice example-b's ROAS. I recommend raising its share of the shared pool from $50 to $60 (+20%). The step is small enough not to disturb its stable learning state, and the total stays at $100. If the platform only lets you set the single shared pool cap, leave that cap at $100 and apply this as the intended allocation, for example through a campaign spend limit. Do not set the shared cap itself to 60."
