    "reason": "The $100 budget is shared with example-a. example-b spent about $50/day for 30 days at a ROAS of 1.8 ($90 revenue on $50 spend) and a CPA of $25. Its CPA, click volume and impressions are identical to example-a's, so its weaker return comes from lower revenue per conversion ($45 vs $100). I recommend cutting its share of the shared pool from $50 to $40 (-20%) and moving that $10 to example-a, which keeps the total at $100. I did not recommend pausing it because I don't know your break-even ROAS. If 1.8 is above break-even, it is still profitable and can keep a reduced share. If it is below break-even, cut further. As with example-a, apply this as an allocation or spend limit, not as the shared cap itself."
